                            {
                                "target_word": "sponge",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5151cfe-ab1f-3bdb-a133-8eac8eade94f",
                                        "entry_id": "c99b5c0d-1636-3caa-a746-a06e4463657e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To take advantage of the kindness of others."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca6fe914-22e2-4f93-be99-e86ded9a5a80",
                                                "sense_id": "b5151cfe-ab1f-3bdb-a133-8eac8eade94f",
                                                "text": "The fly is an intruder, and a common smell-feast, that spunges upon other Peoples Trenchers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8b8e2f1-9b3e-4050-acdb-81584e8ec293",
                                                "sense_id": "b5151cfe-ab1f-3bdb-a133-8eac8eade94f",
                                                "text": "You can’t go on spunging upon the women."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6de0508f-d52a-4e05-9265-afa18537affe",
                                                "sense_id": "b5151cfe-ab1f-3bdb-a133-8eac8eade94f",
                                                "text": "He has been sponging off his friends for a month now."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c43609f-2056-3344-97fd-91ca22cea924",
                                        "entry_id": "c99b5c0d-1636-3caa-a746-a06e4463657e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To get by imposition; to scrounge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa37799b-cb73-47c4-9bd8-7f99b711366a",
                                                "sense_id": "2c43609f-2056-3344-97fd-91ca22cea924",
                                                "text": "“[…] They talk of you as if you were Croesus—and I expect the beggars sponge on you unconscionably.” And Vickers launched forth into a tirade very different from his platform utterances. He spoke with extreme contempt of the dense stupidity exhibited on all occasions by the working classes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ceff8a2-4993-45f5-99a7-5e692f6cdfb3",
                                                "sense_id": "2c43609f-2056-3344-97fd-91ca22cea924",
                                                "text": "July 17 1735, Jonathan Swift, letter to Lord Ornery\nI am an utter stranger to the persons and places, except when half a score come to sponge on me every Sunday evening"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de4aa438-29bc-43cf-bae0-2b8496b3d330",
                                                "sense_id": "2c43609f-2056-3344-97fd-91ca22cea924",
                                                "text": "to sponge a breakfast"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc32794e-cfa8-3dd5-b44d-c254f802d733",
                                        "entry_id": "c99b5c0d-1636-3caa-a746-a06e4463657e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To deprive (somebody) of something by imposition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7fc9135-0953-4da9-be66-c8200d0b6ce3",
                                                "sense_id": "dc32794e-cfa8-3dd5-b44d-c254f802d733",
                                                "text": "How came such multitudes of our nation […] to be sponged of their plate and their money?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "95257583-6168-31da-83da-ee87a96b519b",
                                        "entry_id": "c99b5c0d-1636-3caa-a746-a06e4463657e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To clean, soak up, or dab with a sponge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dfdaf99c-38ec-3323-9387-b3297f33309b",
                                        "entry_id": "c99b5c0d-1636-3caa-a746-a06e4463657e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To suck in, or imbibe, like a sponge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52d5c4d9-f4da-31f2-a279-7fb558826301",
                                        "entry_id": "c99b5c0d-1636-3caa-a746-a06e4463657e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To wipe out with a sponge, as letters or writing; to efface; to destroy all trace of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b095eb81-9297-4c42-a80d-7bc1451ecfc1",
                                                "sense_id": "52d5c4d9-f4da-31f2-a279-7fb558826301",
                                                "text": "Lett the eyes which have looked on Idols, sponge out their unlawfull acts"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78e51b49-a2ec-30c8-ac50-47c498ef6710",
                                        "entry_id": "c99b5c0d-1636-3caa-a746-a06e4463657e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be converted, as dough, into a light, spongy mass by the agency of yeast or leaven."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "652a0622-6417-3d58-8bfa-77ad4516afca",
                                        "entry_id": "c99b5c0d-1636-3caa-a746-a06e4463657e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To use a piece of wild sponge as a tool when foraging for food."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of dolphins"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5944861f-54de-4c84-9c85-4699647dad9f",
                                                "sense_id": "652a0622-6417-3d58-8bfa-77ad4516afca",
                                                "text": "Why do dolphins sponge instead of foraging in a more \"normal\" way?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab09a301-28f1-4a6c-8586-52e83af7acaa",
                                                "sense_id": "652a0622-6417-3d58-8bfa-77ad4516afca",
                                                "text": "Sponging is worth thinking about in some detail because it illustrates many of the challenges and sources of controversy in studying social learning and culture in wild cetaceans."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a6bb86c-dd98-4878-91b7-19bd3be8e1d0",
                                                "sense_id": "652a0622-6417-3d58-8bfa-77ad4516afca",
                                                "text": "Moreover, the females that do it seem to \"sponge\" relentlessly throughout the day, hunting more than other females and more than male spongers too."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
